# shellcheck configuration for the udept source tree.
# https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/wiki/Directive
#
# CI enforces `shellcheck --severity=error src/dep` — so warnings
# and below do not block builds. This file is for the developer
# running `shellcheck src/dep` locally without the --severity flag
# and wanting a low-noise baseline.
#
# Two patterns in src/dep.in are deliberately not shellcheck-clean and
# are covered by inline `# shellcheck disable=...` directives at the
# source site:
#
#   - SC2104 at handle_arg_info: `continue` propagates from a function
#     up to the caller's enclosing argv `for` loop (POSIX-defined).
#   - SC2151 across comm_float / comm_ver: negative-return-as-signed-
#     magnitude via bash's mod-256 truncation (-1 -> 255). Documented
#     at the function header; vercmp() reads `$? >= 128` as "less than".
#
# Warning-level findings (--severity=warning surfaces ~92 across
# SC2046, SC2206, SC2155, SC2128, etc.) are tracked for a future
# cleanup pass. Many sit in word-splitting / IFS-split patterns the
# original author leaned on deliberately; mechanical fixes would
# regress behaviour. Triage TBD.
